course: dictionary
lesson: 1374
title: What something can do
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A capability is the ability or power to do something. When you read it, look at the words around it. They are the context, and they tell you what the capability is. «The robot has the capability to climb stairs.» The sentence says the robot can climb stairs, so capability means its power to do that.
explain: Capabilities (with an s) are the skills, tools or strength that someone or something has. «The tablet has the capabilities of a small computer» means it can do many of the things a computer can do. Ask yourself: what can it do? That question is your clue.
explain: You will also hear phrases like «within your capabilities» and «beyond its capabilities». Within your capabilities means you are able to do it. Beyond its capabilities means it is too hard for it. Try putting your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Capability means the ability or power to do something.
fact: Capabilities means the skills, tools or strength someone or something has.
fact: In science and technology lessons, machines and computers are often compared by their capabilities.
fact: «Within your capabilities» means you are able to do it.
fact: «Beyond its capabilities» means it is too hard for it to do.
exercise: «The robot has the capability to climb stairs.» What does capability mean here? | A loud noise | *The ability or power to do something | A type of robot toy | A rule that stops robots
exercise: «The tablet has the capabilities of a small computer.» What are capabilities? | *Skills, tools or strength it has | Its owner's name | Bright colours on the screen | A place where it is kept
exercise: Sam says, «That climb is beyond my capabilities.» What does Sam mean? | The climb is his favourite game | *The climb is too hard for him to do | He will climb it with a friend | He has climbed it many times
test: «Finishing this puzzle is within your capabilities.» What does within your capabilities mean? | *Something you are able to do | Something that costs money | Something you must never try | Something only grown-ups can do
test: Which list best shows the capabilities of a computer? | *Its speed, its memory and what it can do | Its colour and its shape | Its name and its owner | The room it sits in
exam: «The rover's capabilities include digging and taking photos.» What does capabilities mean here? | *Its skills and tools, such as digging and taking photos | Its paint colour | The number of wheels it has only | Its owner's name
